      "side": 1,
      "message": "`Arc\u003cMutex\u003c_\u003e\u003e` unfortunately doesn\u0027t work due to the way the starlark crate is designed.\n\nIn the evaluator, the context is stored here:\n`pub extra_mut: Option\u003c\u0026\u0027a mut dyn AnyLifetime\u003c\u0027e\u003e\u003e,`\n\nSince it is a reference rather than an actual object, we are unable to detect when `extra_mut` is dropped in order to release the lock. Also, the `Evaluator` object has no callabck mechanisms like drop hooks or anything.\n\n`Cow` doesn\u0027t work because we need to read the mutations at times to verify that the mutation was correct.",
